  "projectStory": "Project story\n项目页面无其他语言可用。\n创作者\nSol Bird\n了解更多联系\n类别\n艺术\n标签\nother\n支持信息\n众筹风险\n了解更多\nImperial Crane Teacup: A Masterpiece of Tradition and Craftsmanship\nIn the heart of traditional Chinese culture, where the art of tea-making mirrors the pursuit of harmony and wisdom, emerges the \"Imperial Crane Teacup.\" This exquisite creation, now seeking your support on Indiegogo, is more than a teacup; it's a bridge between the ancient artistry of the East and the tranquil moments of your tea ritual. Crafted for those who cherish the serene tranquility of tea drinking, this teacup elevates every sip into an experience of imperial grandeur and elegance.\nCraftsmanship\nEach \"Imperial Crane Teacup\" is a labor of love and skill, born from the hands of artisans who have inherited techniques. The teacup showcases the esteemed crafts of silver lining, cloisonné, imitation lacquer, and gilding—each contributing to its unparalleled beauty and durability. The teacup is a testament to meticulous craftsmanship, marrying the profound heritage of Chinese artistry with extraordinary aesthetic appeal.\nSilver Water Benefits\nEach teacup is lined with pure silver. Silver can purify water and disinfect it. A South Korean study published in a 2008 edition of \"Journal of Microbiology and Biotechnology\" found that ionic silver solutions are effective at killing bacteria and Candida albicans fungus in Petri dishes. University of North Texas researcher Dr. Mark Farinha found that solutions of colloidal silver had an antimicrobial effect on in-situ populations of Staphylococcus, Candida and Pseudomonas.  \nThe benefits of silver were known by the earliest civilizations with an oligodynamic (germ-killing) effect. As it became better understood how micro-organisms such as bacteria, viruses and molds caused disease and spoilage, more emphasis was put on discovering and using substances that killed them. \nSymbolic Design\nAdorned with an elegant white crane in flight, set against a rare purple backdrop, the teacup symbolizes longevity, peace, and freedom. This striking design, complemented by golden clouds signifying harmony, invites you into a world where each tea-drinking session is a moment of zen.\nThe interior's silver lining and the rim's delicate gilding finish ensure that the essence and purity of your tea are impeccably preserved, adding a contemporary flair to the classic design.\nSustainability\nExperience daily hydration in its healthiest and most sophisticated form. A warm cup of tea will always be there to jump-start your morning or calm down your afternoon.\nOur commitment to sustainability is reflected in the eco-friendly materials and practices used in creating the \"Imperial Crane Teacup.\" We believe in honoring our planet as much as we honor our traditions.\nSpecifications\nDiameter: 6.4cm\nHeight: 5.3cm\nCapacity: 120ml\nBy pledging to the \"Imperial Crane Teacup\" on Indiegogo, you're not just acquiring a piece of art; you're supporting the preservation of traditional craftsmanship and taking a stand for sustainable practices. Your support will help us continue this journey, expanding our line of products and exploring new ways to blend tradition with modern aesthetics.\nPledge today and become part of this exquisite journey!",
